~ bed
Traveller: Not my bed. He'll be at the forge till dark — he won't miss it.
=> END

~ woke
Traveller: ...That's better. First proper sleep since the boat.
=> END

~ bed_again
Traveller: [[He still won't miss it.|Not the first time.|His loss.]]
=> END

~ woke_again
Traveller: [[Morning.|Up, then.|Slept like a stone.]]
=> END

~ chair
Traveller: A good chair. Somebody sat here a long time, wearing it in.
=> END

~ hearth
The fire is banked low, the way you leave it when you mean to be back. Warm on your hands.
=> END

~ desk
Ledgers, in a careful hand. Iron bought, tools sold, a debt or two crossed through.
Nothing about the road.
=> END

~ swords
Two blades on the rack, oiled and keen, and not for sale. He keeps his best.
=> END

~ barrel
The water is black with scale. A sword stands in it, cooling. He has not been gone long.
=> END

~ crates
Nails, hinges, a horseshoe or two. The ordinary weight of a trade.
=> END
